WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.854
Julia frowned at Brody. Heracles was definitely intimidating as an athlete.

2
00:00:06.855 --> 00:00:12.258
But Heracles was a kid, just like them. And he seemed like a nice guy.

3
00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:17.187
"Maybe we should talk to Hermes about a strategy," she suggested.

4
00:00:17.188 --> 00:00:22.325
"Now that he's seen Heracles, he must realize that no mortal will ever beat him.

5
00:00:22.326 --> 00:00:26.238
Maybe he'll even let us go home before the Games."

6
00:00:26.239 --> 00:00:34.608
"Never," Markos stated. "The gods don't give up easily. Especially when it comes to the Games."

7
00:00:34.609 --> 00:00:41.529
"Well, I don't give up either." Brody declared suddenly. He puffed out his chest.

8
00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:47.751
"I'm going to beat Heracles, even if I have to train nonstop between now and the Games."

9
00:00:47.752 --> 00:00:54.749
Julia stared at him. "Are you crazy? A minute ago you were worried about competing against him.

10
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.636
And you saw what Heracles did!" she added.

11
00:00:58.637 --> 00:01:03.819
"He outran a horse! And picked up a giant ram!"

12
00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:11.319
Brody looked stubborn. "I don't have a choice, Julia. And if I keep up the training, I can do it."

13
00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:16.858
Julia shook her head. "This doesn't seem like a real plan, Brody."

14
00:01:16.859 --> 00:01:24.493
"Yeah, well, until you come up with something better, this is what I'm going to do," he shot back.

15
00:01:24.494 --> 00:01:28.929
Julia stomped off to get away from Brody for a few minutes.

16
00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:34.115
This situation was bad, and he didn't even seem to realize it.

17
00:01:34.116 --> 00:01:39.531
All this time she'd been hoping Brody could actually win at the Games.

18
00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:48.466
But now that he was competing against Heracles, she was sure Brody—along with all the other athletes—was going to lose. Unless

19
00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:54.785
the gods managed to sabotage Heracles. Then Brody might have a chance. As

20
00:01:54.786 --> 00:02:00.387
she walked around, she could hear people talking about Heracles. Everyone

21
00:02:00.388 --> 00:02:05.423
still seemed dazzled by Zeus' amazing hero. Then

22
00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:08.845
there was a commotion somewhere near the dais. Julia

23
00:02:08.846 --> 00:02:14.976
looked over there just in time to see Heracles lift Zeus by one ankle! The

24
00:02:14.977 --> 00:02:19.415
king of the gods waved as the crowd cheered. "Behold

25
00:02:19.416 --> 00:02:26.703
the greatest mortal athlete of all time!" Zeus called out. Suddenly

26
00:02:26.704 --> 00:02:33.478
someone grabbed Julia's arm. "Let go," she snapped, yanking it back. She

27
00:02:33.479 --> 00:02:41.482
turned around, expecting to see Brody. Instead Aphrodite was standing there! Julia

28
00:02:41.483 --> 00:02:50.160
gasped. "I—I'm sorry," she babbled. "I thought my friends were . . ." She

29
00:02:50.161 --> 00:02:56.250
was afraid that the goddess would be angry at the way Julia had spoken to her. But

30
00:02:56.251 --> 00:03:02.183
Aphrodite just looked excited. She was staring at Heracles. "Do

31
00:03:02.184 --> 00:03:13.577
you see Zeus' hero, mortal girl?" the goddess said. "I've never seen a mortal so handsome!" "Um

32
00:03:13.578 --> 00:03:21.291
. . ." Julia wasn't sure what to say to that. "He's handsome, I guess." Luckily

33
00:03:21.292 --> 00:03:28.563
Aphrodite didn't seem to care about Julia's reply. She grabbed a passing woman. "Isn't

34
00:03:28.564 --> 00:03:38.757
this exciting?" Aphrodite said. "The Games should be quite interesting this year. Don't you agree, mortal woman?" Julia

35
00:03:38.758 --> 00:03:46.199
slipped out of Aphrodite's view, relieved that she hadn't accidentally offended the goddess. After

36
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:52.484
Aphrodite's trick with the poisoned chiton, Julia didn't want to take any chances. Hera

37
00:03:52.485 --> 00:03:56.815
and Aphrodite made her especially nervous. A

38
00:03:56.816 --> 00:04:02.583
moment later she saw Brody and Markos coming toward her. "You

39
00:04:02.584 --> 00:04:09.994
missed it!" Brody said. "We just heard Ares and Dionysus talking about Heracles." "Oh?"

40
00:04:09.995 --> 00:04:16.319
Julia glanced at the dais. Heracles had lowered Zeus to the ground. Now

41
00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:25.321
the hero was doing a one-handed handstand while he used his feet to balance a nervous-looking goat. "Yes,"

42
00:04:25.322 --> 00:04:33.645
Markos said. "The gods were trying to figure out a way to sabotage Heracles before the Games." "And

43
00:04:33.646 --> 00:04:39.466
after that, we passed Hermes talking to Artemis and Apollo," Brody said. "They

44
00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:46.367
were plotting too." He laughed, looking a bit more cheerful now. "It

45
00:04:46.368 --> 00:04:51.087
sounds like all the gods are making plans to sabotage Heracles." "That's

46
00:04:51.088 --> 00:04:55.987
good for you, for two reasons," Markos told him. "One,

47
00:04:55.988 --> 00:05:04.676
the gods probably won't keep plotting against you, even though you're one of the best mortal athletes in the Games." "Thanks,

48
00:05:04.677 --> 00:05:10.465
dude." Brody grinned broadly. "What's the second reason?" "Duh."

49
00:05:10.466 --> 00:05:20.796
Julia rolled her eyes. "The second reason is they might actually succeed in getting Heracles out of the Games." "Oh,

50
00:05:20.797 --> 00:05:26.293
right." Brody grinned. "Then I can definitely win!" Suddenly

51
00:05:26.294 --> 00:05:32.479
they heard a loud gasp from the crowd. Julia glanced at the dais. The

52
00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:37.679
goat on Heracles' feet had turned into white-hot flames! "Hephaestus!"

53
00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:43.751
Zeus thundered. He pointed at the flames. Twin

54
00:05:43.752 --> 00:05:50.244
lightning bolts shot out of his fingers, and a second later the flames sizzled and disappeared. Heracles

55
00:05:50.245 --> 00:05:54.038
let his legs fall, and then he stood up. "Thank

56
00:05:54.039 --> 00:06:03.073
you, Zeus," he said, bowing. His feet were blackened from the fire, but he didn't show any signs of pain. Zeus

57
00:06:03.074 --> 00:06:08.097
was glaring at a god Julia hadn't seen before. But

58
00:06:08.098 --> 00:06:16.098
based on the god's name—Hephaestus—Julia knew he was the god of fire and the forge. "How

59
00:06:16.099 --> 00:06:22.268
dare you tamper with my hero?" Zeus thundered. Just

60
00:06:22.269 --> 00:06:27.714
then Hera stepped into view behind Hephaestus. "What's

61
00:06:27.715 --> 00:06:34.184
the matter, husband?" she asked in a voice that sent a chill through Julia. "Are

62
00:06:34.185 --> 00:06:41.710
you afraid your hero isn't mighty enough to handle a few friendly pranks?" "Friendly?"

63
00:06:41.711 --> 00:06:48.035
Zeus repeated, shifting his dark glare to her. Hera

64
00:06:48.036 --> 00:06:56.281
took a few steps backward. "You'll soon see just how un friendly I can be, wife!"

65
00:06:56.282 --> 00:07:01.573
With a deafening thunderclap, he and Heracles both disappeared.

66
00:07:01.574 --> 00:07:07.982
Julia shuddered. "Wow, things are getting serious."

67
00:07:07.983 --> 00:07:17.695
"Yeah, did you see the way Zeus shot that fire right off Heracles' feet?" Brody exclaimed. "It was cool!"

68
00:07:17.696 --> 00:07:21.545
"This isn't a video game, Brody!" Julia snapped.

69
00:07:21.546 --> 00:07:26.063
"We're all in big danger here." She turned to Markos.

70
00:07:26.064 --> 00:07:34.201
"Zeus is obviously guarding Heracles closely. What if the gods don't succeed in getting Heracles out of the Games?"

71
00:07:34.202 --> 00:07:41.683
"Stop worrying, Julia. I'll beat him!" Brody declared. He flexed his muscles.

72
00:07:41.684 --> 00:07:46.899
Julia ignored him as she waited for Markos' reply.

73
00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:52.339
"Zeus is powerful," Markos answered. "But he's only one god.

74
00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:57.960
The other gods can band together to outwit him. They will probably succeed."

75
00:07:57.961 --> 00:08:02.759
"I hope you're right," Julia said slowly.

76
00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:15.579
But as she watched Hera cross the dais, Julia felt a fresh wave of worry. What lay ahead for all of them?

